211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (These systems involve small numbers of pigs, typically up to 10 in number. Pigs in this system are raised primarily for household consumption or supply of pork to local markets. This system generally entails minimal investment, it tends to be characterised by inadequate housing. The reliance on scavenging for food by pigs in these systems can lead to nutritional deficiencies and increased susceptibility to diseases.7)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
