226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A What kind of solid, liquid and gaseous waste is generated by piggery establishments and what is the pollution potential arising thereby? Piggery operations generate significant waste, including dung, carcasses, leftover feed, and cleaning wastewater. This paper analyzes the state of pollution on the ground, the waste discarded, current management methods, and the resulting impact on soil, water, and air.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (B. How does inadequate waste management by piggery establishments affect public health and safety? The paper explores what the consequences of poor waste management on public health and safety may manifest as. Specifically, the incidence of diseases that may arise from mismanagement of piggery waste is detailed. These comprise direct pathways through which piggery waste management ties to human health. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (C. What indirect risks are associated with waste management at piggery establishments? The paper delves into the relationship between pigs being reared in high density environments which are unhygienic and the heightened potential for 6 non-therapeutic antibiotic usage. Indiscriminate antibiotic usage may give rise to antimicrobial resistance \(AMR\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
