/T (Untreated Wastewater Discarded in Drains: This header assesses whether untreated wastewater generated from piggery operations was improperly disposed of into public drainage systems, which could result in significant environmental pollution and public health risks due to the introduction of pathogens and nutrients into urban waterways. Faecal contamination of public drains leads to several invasive and antibiotic resistant organisms such as Salmonella enterica serovar Typhimurium. This pathogen, a known cause of Typhoid fever, poses a significant threat to human health.12)
/E (Untreated Wastewater Discarded in Drains: This header assesses whether untreated wastewater generated from piggery operations was improperly disposed of into public drainage systems, which could result in significant environmental pollution and public health risks due to the introduction of pathogens and nutrients into urban waterways. Faecal contamination of public drains leads to several invasive and antibiotic resistant organisms such as Salmonella enterica serovar Typhimurium. This pathogen, a known cause of Typhoid fever, poses a significant threat to human health.12)
/Pg 15 0 R
