276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (During the study conducted on ground, the methodology employed for carcass collection and disposal could be observed at 38 out of 146 units. Each of these 38 units were found to employ inappropriate carcass disposal practices, raising serious biosecurity concerns and increasing the risk of disease transmission and environmental contamination. The accumulation of organic waste, including carcasses and effluent byproducts, often exceeds the absorptive capacity of the surrounding environment, leading to risks such as leachate formation, nitrate infiltration, and habitat disruption. This reflects a systemic failure to implement even the most basic sanitary and biosecurity protocols, highlighting a disturbing lack of accountability and a blatant disregard for both animal welfare and environmental health standards.)
/E (During the study conducted on ground, the methodology employed for carcass collection and disposal could be observed at 38 out of 146 units. Each of these 38 units were found to employ inappropriate carcass disposal practices, raising serious biosecurity concerns and increasing the risk of disease transmission and environmental contamination. The accumulation of organic waste, including carcasses and effluent byproducts, often exceeds the absorptive capacity of the surrounding environment, leading to risks such as leachate formation, nitrate infiltration, and habitat disruption. This reflects a systemic failure to implement even the most basic sanitary and biosecurity protocols, highlighting a disturbing lack of accountability and a blatant disregard for both animal welfare and environmental health standards.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
