<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This study concludes that piggery operations in India pose severe and escalating risks to public health and environment integrity, stemming from the unchecked proliferation of units operating with limited regulatory framework. The indiscriminate disposal of manure, slurry, carcasses, and biomedical waste contributes to significant air, water, and soil pollution, manifesting in the contamination of surface and groundwater sources and  the unchecked release of  hazardous  gases  such as methane, ammonia and)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
