/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Ultimately, the continued tolerance of unregulated piggery operations permits widespread environmental degradation and endangers vulnerable human populations, including children and elderly living in proximity who face heightened risk of respiratory illness, enteric infections, and vector-borne diseases, under the pretext of economic activity. Only through coordinated environmental and epidemiological intervention can the hidden health externalities of this sector be contained, ensuring cleaner air, safer water, and dignified living conditions for all. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T ( 5.2. Specific Policy Recommendations )
/E ( 5.2. Specific Policy Recommendations )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The following recommendations emphasize the need for improved waste management policies. By implementing these strategies, stakeholders can work collaboratively to minimize environmental impacts, safeguard public health, and promote the long-term sustainability of piggery units across India. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T <412E2043656E7472616C20476F7665726E6D656E742085204D696E6973747279206F6620456E7669726F6E6D656E742C20466F7265737420616E6420436C696D617465204368616E676520>
/E <412E2043656E7472616C20476F7665726E6D656E742085204D696E6973747279206F6620456E7669726F6E6D656E742C20466F7265737420616E6420436C696D617465204368616E676520>
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (i. Include Piggery Sector in Environmental Impact Assessment \(EIA\) Regulations: Bring large-scale piggeries under the purview of the EIA Notification under the EPA, 1986, given their proven impact on air, water, and soil quality.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ii. Promote Composting and Biochar Production: Encourage piggery units to adopt composting and biochar technologies for on-site waste treatment, reducing pathogen loads and producing organic soil amendments.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (B. Central Pollution Control Board \(CPCB\))
/E (B. Central Pollution Control Board \(CPCB\))
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (22)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (i. Urgent Reclassification of Piggeries: The current Pollution Index \(PI\) assigned to piggery units \(PI: 50\) is dangerously misleading. At present, the piggery industry has not been scored for wastewater and biomedical waste. As such, an accurate assessment would very likely lead to higher PI for piggery units. CPCB must carry out an assessment after an accurate on ground sample and revise the classification accordingly. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ii. Develop and Notify Comprehensive Environmental Guidelines for Piggeries: Drawing from existing guidelines for poultry and dairy units, CPCB must create enforceable standards or guidelines on Consent to Establish \(CTE\) and Consent to Operate \(CTO\) requirements and procedures. Additionally, effluent treatment, solid waste handling, odour control mechanisms and measures for bioaerosol and particulate matter containment should be detailed in Guidelines of this nature. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iii. Mandate Environmental Monitoring and Reporting: Requirement should be placed on all piggery units to maintain and publicly disclose logs on waste generation, treatment, carcass disposal, and antibiotic/hormone usage. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iv. Integrate Nutrient Recovery and Solid-Liquid Separation Systems: Mandate or incentivize the use of nutrient recovery technologies and solidliquid separators for large and medium-scale units to reduce water pollution and enable the transport of stabilized manure solids.)
/Pg 30 0 R
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (C. State Pollution Control Boards \(SPCBs\))
/E (C. State Pollution Control Boards \(SPCBs\))
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (i. Strict Enforcement of Consent Mechanisms: No piggery unit should be allowed to operate without a valid CTE/CTO. SPCBs must routinely inspect piggery units and impose penalties or closures for non-compliance.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ii. Monitor and Regulate Air and Water Emissions: Enforce statutory standards on ammonia, methane, and hydrogen sulphide emissions; and ensure wastewater treatment complies with norms under the Water Act.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iii. Public Grievance Mechanism: Establish online platforms where communities affected by nearby piggeries can lodge complaints regarding foul odour, fly infestation, or contamination.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (23)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iv. Implement Guidelines for Scientific Disposal of Food Waste: Ensure implementation of Mechanism/Guidelines for Control of Pollution and Enforcement of Environment Norms at Individual Establishments and the Area/ Cluster of Restaurants/ Hotels/ Motels/ Banquets etc, 2020 to ensure that the use of leftover food waste as pig feed is curbed. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (v. Integrate Internet of Things and Real-Time Monitoring: Encourage the adoption of low-cost IoT systems to monitor waste storage and discharge, enabling real-time compliance checks.)
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (D. Urban Local Bodies and State Animal Husbandry Departments)
/E (D. Urban Local Bodies and State Animal Husbandry Departments)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (i. Zoning and Land Use Controls: Establish and enforce siting restrictions for piggery units to ensure they are not located within 200 meters of residential areas, schools, hospitals, or water sources. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ii. Mandatory Sanitary Infrastructure: Requirement to be placed on all piggery units to install closed drainage systems, use waste segregation bins \(biodegradable, biomedical, and carcass waste\) and ensure overed storage for feed and carcasses to control vector breeding. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iii. Facilitate Composting and Treated Water Reuse: Support units to set up composting areas and assess the reuse of treated wastewater for irrigation or as liquid fertilizer inputs.)
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
