354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (i. Adopt Circular Economy Models: Invest in bio-digesters, microalgaebased wastewater treatment \(as per Nagarajan et al., 2019\), and composting systems to minimize ecological harm and recover energy or manure from waste. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ii. Discontinue Hazardous Practices: Stop the use of non-therapeutic antibiotics and heavy metals such as copper and zinc in feed, which have been found to contaminate the food chain and degrade soil health. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iii. Humane and Scientific Carcass Disposal: Implement lime burial or approved incineration technologies. Carcasses must never be dumped in open drains or fed to dogs, which violates both public health standards and basic decency. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iv. Health and Safety Compliance: Equip workers with PPE, conduct periodic health check-ups, and provide training on sanitation, disease prevention, and humane handling of animals.)
/Pg 32 0 R
>>
endobj
