359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Zoonotic Disease Surveillance: Monitor and report incidences of zoonotic infections linked to piggery waste and bioaerosols, with focus particularly on swine-origin pathogens such as Salmonella, E. coli, and Listeria. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ii. Combat Antimicrobial Resistance \(AMR\): Regulate antibiotic usage in piggery operations. Routine feed additives must not be utilised unless prescribed by a registered veterinarian. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (iii. Test Groundwater and Soil Near Piggeries: Establish regular testing regimes for groundwater and soil quality, especially where carcass pits or slurry ponds are used.)
/Pg 32 0 R
>>
